ANGLE: this is a POSIX system, not a Linux one.

ENABLE_WEBGL=ON (so WebGL can run on Mesa's llvmpipe) compiles the bundled
ANGLE for the first time in this port, and its GTK platform file hardcodes
ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX for every non-Apple, non-Windows build.  On this system
that reaches for things it does not have:

    src/common/SimpleMutex.cpp:17:18: fatal error: linux/futex.h:
      No such file or directory

  - PlatformGTK.cmake: define ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX only when CMake says the
    target is Linux.  common/platform.h then classifies the system itself.
  - platform.h: add __LIKEOS__ to the POSIX list so that classification
    succeeds (the fallthrough is `#error Unsupported platform`).
  - Display.cpp: the EGL/GLX display backends are selected by
    ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX; they are exactly what this X11-on-Mesa port needs,
    so admit __LIKEOS__ alongside it.
  - log_utils.h, system_utils.h: the sysroot's libstdc++ is built without
    wchar_t support, so std::wostream/std::wstring do not exist.  Only the
    Windows paths ever use them; compile them out where the library lacks
    them.
  - Display.cpp, second part: the EGL_ANGLE_platform_angle_device_type_egl
    client extension is likewise enabled only for ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX.
    WebKitGTK asks for exactly that device type when it creates its ANGLE
    display, and ANGLE's validation answered EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE before any
    driver code ran -- WebGL "disabled or unavailable" on every page, with
    nothing logged (found with user/bin/tests/anglecheck.cpp).

--- a/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/PlatformGTK.cmake
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/PlatformGTK.cmake
@@ -1,4 +1,10 @@
-list(APPEND ANGLE_DEFINITIONS ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX EGL_NO_PLATFORM_SPECIFIC_TYPES USE_SYSTEM_EGL)
+# ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX only where that is true: common/platform.h detects
+# every POSIX system by its own macros, and forcing the wrong platform makes
+# SimpleMutex reach for a kernel futex header the system does not have.
+if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux")
+    list(APPEND ANGLE_DEFINITIONS ANGLE_PLATFORM_LINUX)
+endif ()
+list(APPEND ANGLE_DEFINITIONS EGL_NO_PLATFORM_SPECIFIC_TYPES USE_SYSTEM_EGL)
 include(linux.cmake)
 
 if (USE_OPENGL)
--- a/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/src/common/log_utils.h
+++ b/Source/ThirdParty/ANGLE/src/common/log_utils.h
@@ -136,10 +136,15 @@
         return FmtHexAutoSized(os, fmt.mValue, fmt.mPrefix, "0x", '0');
     }
 
+#if !defined(__GLIBCXX__) || defined(_GLIBCXX_USE_WCHAR_T)
+    // Wide streams exist only where the C++ library was built with wchar_t
+    // support; a libstdc++ configured without it has no std::wostream to
+    // overload for.  Only the Windows paths ever format into wide streams.
     friend std::wostream &operator<<(std::wostream &wos, const FmtHexHelper &fmt)
     {
         return FmtHexAutoSized(wos, fmt.mValue, fmt.mPrefix, L"0x", L'0');
     }
+#endif
 };
 
 }  // namespace priv
